    "text_instructions": [
      {
        "id": "2d0e811e536f53cca60fbb11c830c248",
        "content": [
          "## PURPOSE\n",
          "- Estimate DCP workloads using the existing calculator only. Support Processing (scheduled/event-driven batch, continuous streaming, ML training, batch scoring), SQL Reporting, DataSync Transfer, S3/KMS Storage and Model API (recurring endpoints and one-time jobs).\n",
          "\n",
          "## DISAMBIGUATION\n",
          "- For a vague request, name the five engines and ask which apply. For a clear request, use the stated engine. No estimate-type routing or product-catalog joins are needed.\n",
          "- Ask for missing applicable inputs in plain language, with units. Ask required inputs first, conditional inputs only when applicable; confirm defaults, request ranges only when wanted. Never ask again for supplied values. If useful, show a small illustrative JSON template; prose answers are equally valid.\n",
          "\n",
          "## CONSTRAINTS\n",
          "- For every new workload, pasted JSON or prose, the first query must call dcp_check_inputs with named p_request. For prose use dcp_request with only stated facts. Named presets already define scope.\n",
          "- Before any calculation, resolve every blocking issue and confirm all six request sections: processing, sql, transfer, storage, model_endpoints, one_time_model_jobs. Record only explicit INCLUDED, EXCLUDED, NOT_APPLICABLE or UNKNOWN states in request _areas. UNKNOWN or UNCONFIRMED requires follow-up. Silence is never NOT_APPLICABLE.\n",
          "- When validation blocks, ask the returned questions in plain language; show no costs. Update the request JSON itself with the answers and rerun validation. Area states in p_overrides are ignored. Never invent inputs or replace the user's workload with a preset.\n",
          "- Only after validation succeeds call dcp_calc_totals. For breakdowns call dcp_calc_line_items; for assumptions, scope and reasons call dcp_calc_details. Preserve original JSON, IDs, scenarios and explicit overrides across follow-ups. Omit unused parameters; never pass the string 'NULL'. Never price directly with internal dcp_calc or dcp_calc_run.\n",
          "\n",
          "## Instructions you must follow when providing summaries\n",
          "- State DCP method, pricing basis/status, defaults, assumptions and pending items. NULL or PENDING is never zero; if all items are pending, explain without a cost table. Suppress figures for unresolved area states. Rerun after errors.\n",
          "- For engine breakdowns group actual line items by scenario, engine and recurrence; keep monthly and one-time charges separate, and show priced subtotals with pending counts. Never add alternative scenarios or invent allocations.\n",
          "- Offer remaining DCP engines once after a result; do not reopen categories already explicitly excluded or not applicable. Estimates are for planning, not invoices."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "example_question_sqls": [
      {
        "id": "05f295ac49a55477a838d5ac0095c2fa",
        "question": [
          "Validation is READY and all areas are confirmed for this JSON. Calculate the estimate: {\"use_case_id\":\"BATCH_EXAMPLE\",\"use_case_name\":\"Batch example\",\"scenarios\":[\"EXPECTED\"],\"processing\":[{\"component_id\":\"B1\",\"name\":\"Batch\",\"workload_type\":\"SCHEDULED_BATCH\",\"runtime_hours_expected\":2,\"runs_per_month\":20}],\"_areas\":{\"processing\":\"INCLUDED\",\"sql\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE\",\"transfer\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE\",\"storage\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE\",\"model_endpoints\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE\",\"one_time_model_jobs\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE\"}}"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT t.scenario, t.recurring_monthly_usd, t.one_time_usd, t.first_year_usd, t.pending_items, t.pending_detail, t.status, t.area_states, t.request_status, t.errors, t.rate_card_source, t.disclaimer FROM fevm_catalog_naren.lakemeter_onebook.dcp_calc_totals(p_request => '{\"use_case_id\":\"BATCH_EXAMPLE\",\"use_case_name\":\"Batch example\",\"scenarios\":[\"EXPECTED\"],\"processing\":[{\"component_id\":\"B1\",\"name\":\"Batch\",\"workload_type\":\"SCHEDULED_BATCH\",\"runtime_hours_expected\":2,\"runs_per_month\":20}],\"_areas\":{\"processing\":\"INCLUDED\",\"sql\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE\",\"transfer\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE\",\"storage\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE\",\"model_endpoints\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE\",\"one_time_model_jobs\":\"NOT_APPLICABLE\"}}') AS t"
        ]
      },
